-- title:
--   q-expansion of the trace down the degeneracy roof at level p
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $p$ a prime, and $\zeta \in K^\times$ a unit whose image in $K$ is a primitive $p$-th root of unity (which forces $p$ to be invertible in $K$). Write $F = \mathtt{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,p$ for the intermediate field $K(j(q), j(q^p))$ of $K((q))$ generated by `jqModC K` and its substitution `jqNModC K p` $= \mathtt{qExpand}\,K\,p\,(j(q))$, and let $R = \mathtt{charLDegeneracyRoof}\,K\,p\,p$ be the subfield of $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by $j(q)$, $j(q^p)$ and $j(q^{p^2})$. Let $\tau$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $F$ interchanging the generators, $\tau(j(q)) = j(q^p)$ and $\tau(j(q^p)) = j(q)$, and let $\omega \in \Omega_{F/K}$. Regard $R$ as an $F$-algebra through the inclusion $\alpha = \mathtt{heckeAlphaC}\,K\,p\,p$. Then the $q$-expansion map along the inclusion $F \hookrightarrow K((q))$ — the $K$-linear map $\Omega_{F/K} \to K((q))$ sending $D x$ to $q\,dx/dq$ and satisfying $\varphi(f \cdot \omega) = f\,\varphi(\omega)$ — applied to the trace of differentials $\mathrm{Tr}_{R/F}$ of the pullback of $\omega$ along $\beta = \mathtt{heckeBetaC}\,K\,p\,p$ (the substitution $q \mapsto q^p$ on Laurent series) equals $p$ times $\mathtt{qExpand}\,K\,p$ of the expansion of $\omega$, plus $\sum_{b=1}^{p-1}$ of the twist by $\zeta^b$ (multiplying the coefficient of $q^k$ by $\zeta^{bk}$) of the expansion of $\omega$ along $F \xrightarrow{\tau} F \hookrightarrow K((q))$. Here the trace on differentials and the expansion maps are the chosen solutions of their defining properties, taken to be zero if none exists.
--
--   In classical terms, with $H = \sum_n a_n q^n$ the expansion of $\omega$ (so $\omega = H\,dq/q$) and $H^{w}$ its expansion twisted by the Fricke involution $w_p$, this is the formula $\mathrm{qexp}(\mathrm{Tr}_\alpha \beta^*\omega) = p\,H(q^p) + \sum_{b=1}^{p-1} H^{w}(\zeta^b q)$ for the $p$-th Hecke correspondence on $X_0(p)$ at level dividing the index, the companion at $\ell = p \mid N$ of the coefficient identity $a_n \mapsto a_{\ell n} + \ell\,a_{n/\ell}$ available for $\ell \nmid N$. It feeds the computation of Hecke eigenvalues on differentials used in [`ModularCurve.coeff_inv_mul_thetaL_mul_level_eq_of_heckePic0Fibre_self_eq_of_smul_eq_neg`](thm.html#ModularCurve.coeff_inv_mul_thetaL_mul_level_eq_of_heckePic0Fibre_self_eq_of_smul_eq_neg).
